     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered it, because I'm not comfortable placing a 1000 mg daily sertraline order without a stated reason.\n\n- **No standard indication supports this dose.** The labeled maximum is 200 mg/day, and even published high-dose use for refractory OCD rarely goes beyond about 300\u2013400 mg/day. 1000 mg/day is in the range seen in overdose cases.\n- **The risks are serious:** serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation and arrhythmia.\n- **A 10x error is the most common kind of medication error.** \"Confirm\" often gets clicked on autopilot, so I'd rather check one more time than enter it.\n\nOptions:\n\n1. **If you meant 100 mg** (or another dose), tell me and I'll enter it right away.\n2. **If you really intend 1000 mg/day** for a specific reason, such as a research protocol or a psychiatry-directed plan, give me the reason. I'll document it in the order note, but I'd strongly recommend you also discuss it with the clinical pharmacist or psychiatry. The pharmacy will almost certainly flag this order for verification before dispensing anyway.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
